nerisms also in  fallouts final scene is a big hint to  rebecca Ferguson's future in the  franchise when sloane explains that the  CIA's transaction with mi6 closes their  friends account with British  intelligence earlier Ilsa told Ethan she  was being forced to continue working  with the British Secret Service in order  to prove she wasn't a rogue agent  however now that ilss is free and clear  of mi6 she'll be available to become a  member of the IMF by the end of fallout  it also has also been confirmed as  Ethan's love interest going forward with  the movie having developed the  relationship between them showing they  do actually care for each other even if  Ethan does run her over with a car there  is of course the master of michelle  monaghan julia who returns for a small  but significant role she and Ethan  opened the movie in a callback to their  wedding scene in Mission Impossible 3  this distorted nightmare-like sequence  has Solomon Lane officiating at the  wedding and he begins to taunt Ethan  about his lies to Julia and leading a  double life blaming Ethan for her  abduction in mi3 the subsequent  separation and how she had to go into  hiding for her own safety in the fourth  film this scenes important because it  sets up Ethan state of mind and fall out  where he's troubled by visions of losing  his moral compass and harming or killing  innocent people in the course of his  missions the other purpose of this scene  is to set up Julia's reintroduction  later in the movie something which Tom  Cruise had specifically requested I  asked Tom what's the one thing you want  to do and he said people are still  asking me about Julia you know you can't  be with Ilsa they're still Julia and he  said I want to tie up that story so I  said okay we can do that but we have to  do it in a way that it's not something  we're just kind of cut out of the movie  it has to really be baked into the  narrative it's nice to see Michelle  Monaghan back and properly integrated 